    ],
    "introductoryText": "Rescales each chosen number field to the range 0 to 1, so fields measured in different units (prices, percentages, days) can be compared, weighted and added up:\n\nnew value = (value − lowest) / (highest − lowest)\n\nThe lowest value in each field becomes 0 and the highest 1; the chosen fields are replaced, the others pass through unchanged.\n\n- Missing values stay missing and are ignored when finding the lowest and highest.\n- A field whose values are all the same becomes 0, and the block's message names it.\n- Choose number fields only: a text or date field stops the block with a message.\n\nTo get z-scores (mean 0, standard deviation 1) instead, use the Normalise block.",
    "dependencies": "",
